-- title:
--   Pole-chart point off the second component: Gauss ring, p prime
-- statement:
--   Fix a prime $p$ and a nonzero natural number $M$ with $p \mid M$ but $p^2 \nmid M$, and a subgroup $H \le (\mathbb{Z}/M)^\times$ containing every unit that maps to $1$ under the reduction $(\mathbb{Z}/M)^\times \to (\mathbb{Z}/(M/p))^\times$. Assume the $q$-expansion `jqModC ℚ` lies in the field $F(\top) =$ `qExpFunctionFieldC ℚ ⊤`, and let $\mathfrak{X}$ be a model in the sense of the structure `XHDRModelAtP p M H hpM hj` over the base ring `R p` (properness, flatness, integrality, local finite presentation and normality of the two-chart integral model attached to $\Gamma_H(M)$, a smooth proper model at the auxiliary level, a curve model over $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ identified with the generic-fibre base change and pinned on the finite chart, Galois equivariance, and further fields). Let $W_0$ be a valuation subring of $F(\Gamma_H(M)) =$ `qExpFunctionFieldC ℚ (ΓM M H)` pinned by the Gauss condition: $f_0 \in W_0$ iff there are power series $a, a'$ with coefficients in [`GaloisRep.ratLocalizedAt p`](def/GaloisRep_Flat.html#L8) (the rationals with denominator coprime to $p$) such that the reduction of $a'$ modulo $p$, via [`GaloisRep.ratLocalizedAtResidue p`](def/GaloisRep_RatLocalizedAtResidue.html#L15), is nonzero and $f_0 \cdot a' = a$ as Laurent series over $\mathbb{Q}$. Let $A$ be a valuation subring of $\mathrm{AlgebraicClosure}\ \mathbb{Q}$ with $p$ a nonunit of $A$ (the predicate `LiesOverPrime p`), whose residue field is algebraically closed of characteristic $p$, and let $\rho :$ `R p` $\to A$ be a ring homomorphism compatible with the structure map to $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$. Let $y$ be a point of the fibre of `toBase p (ΓM M H) hj` over the residue map $($ `IsLocalRing.residue` $A) \circ \rho$, lying in the image on points of $\mathfrak{X}.\mathrm{comp}\ A\ hA\ \rho\ h\rho\ 0$ but not in that of $\mathfrak{X}.\mathrm{comp}\ A\ hA\ \rho\ h\rho\ 1$, and let $\mathfrak{p}$ be a prime of the pole-chart algebra `chartAlgInf p (ΓM M H) hj` whose image under `ιInf` is the first pullback projection of $y$. The conclusion has three parts: the image of $p$ in the pole-chart algebra lies in $\mathfrak{p}$; for every $s$ in the pole-chart algebra not in $\mathfrak{p}$, the inverse of $s$ in $F(\Gamma_H(M))$ lies in $W_0$; and the ideal generated by $p$ in the localisation of the pole-chart algebra at $\mathfrak{p}$ is prime.
--
--   This records, in the chart at the cusp $j = \infty$, the two local properties of a geometric special-fibre point that lies on one component of the special fibre of the Deligne–Rapoport model of $X_H(M)$ and off the other: the local ring sits inside the Gauss valuation ring $W_0$, and $p$ generates a prime ideal there, so that the fibre is locally integral at the point. It supplies the point hypotheses for the regularity statement about $q$-expansions of cusp forms at such points, and is cited in the proof that integral $q$-expansions give differentials regular away from a finite set of places.
